 "fylite:page": "evolve",
 "fylite:case": {
  "fylite:name": "ITER 15 MA 感应燃烧（解析几何，自足）",
  "fylite:name_en": "ITER 15 MA inductive burn (analytic geometry, self-contained)",
  "fylite:note": "★**不需要任何外部文件**：形状是解析的（a = 2.0 m、R/a = 3.1、κ = 1.70、δ = 0.34、B<sub>0</sub> = 5.3 T），所以这一档随页面就能跑。代价写在页面规矩里：解析几何定不出 ⟨|∇ρ|²/R²⟩，**电流道因此禁用**，q 是规定的、锯齿也就无从触发。要电流道与锯齿，用下面那一档（导入参考平衡）或换到装置几何。★**边界温度 3 keV 是台基顶，不是刮削层**：这一栏没有台基模型，行业里的做法就是解到 ρ≈0.95 并把台基顶当作边界条件——这一档就是那个做法，边界值是你给的一个数，不是解出来的。★成分：铍 1.65 % 隐含 Z<sub>eff</sub> = 1.20，与控件一致；燃料占比 0.375 是 ITER 自己的稀释（n<sub>D</sub> = n<sub>T</sub> = 0.375 n<sub>e</sub>），α 功率按 f² 走，这一项差 1.8 倍。★χ₀ = 0.6 m²/s <strong>不是这一档调出来的</strong>：它来自下面那一档的参考对标，原样搬来。跑到 8 s 时这一档给出 W<sub>th</sub> ≈ 342 MJ、τ<sub>E</sub> ≈ 3.6 s、β<sub>N</sub> ≈ 1.8、Q ≈ 11 —— 与 ITER 15 MA 的设计点同量级，而这几个数<strong>没有被拟合过</strong>。★★它<strong>还在往上走</strong>（dW/dt > 0），而且不会停：常数 χ 对加热功率<strong>没有响应</strong>，于是这个模型里没有燃烧自控——温度升→α 功率升→温度再升。这不是数值发散，是这条闭包的物理后果，也正是「常数 χ 不是预测型闭包」的现场。★<strong>步长受电子—离子交换时标约束</strong>：交换项是显式进算符的，步长长过交换时间不会炸，会让两条热道<strong>悄悄解耦</strong>（本档实测过：自适应把 dt 涨到 0.13 s，T<sub>e</sub> 11.8 keV 对 T<sub>i</sub> 6.3 keV，α 功率只有一半）。所以这一档用固定 dt = 20 ms，页面另有一道以交换时标封顶的闸，封了多少步报在读数里。",
  "fylite:note_en": "★**No external file needed**: the shape is analytic (a = 2.0 m, R/a = 3.1, kappa = 1.70, delta = 0.34, B0 = 5.3 T), so this case runs as the page opens. The price is the page's own rule: analytic geometry does not determine gm2, so the **current channel is disabled**, q is prescribed and no sawtooth can be triggered. For those, use the case below (import a reference equilibrium) or switch to device geometry. ★**The 3 keV boundary is the PEDESTAL TOP, not the scrape-off layer**: this bar has no pedestal model, and the standard practice is to solve to rho about 0.95 with the pedestal top as the boundary condition -- which is what this case does. That number is given, not solved. ★Composition: beryllium at 1.65 % implies Z_eff = 1.20, matching the control; the fuel fraction 0.375 is ITER's own dilution (n_D = n_T = 0.375 n_e), and the alpha power goes as f squared -- a factor 1.8 against pure D-T. ★chi0 = 0.6 m^2/s was <strong>not tuned here</strong>: it comes from the reference benchmark in the case below, carried over unchanged. At 8 s this case gives W_th about 342 MJ, tau_E about 3.6 s, beta_N about 1.8 and Q about 11 -- the same order as the ITER 15 MA design point, and none of those numbers was fitted. ★★It is <strong>still rising</strong> (dW/dt > 0) and it will not stop: a constant chi has <strong>no response to the heating power</strong>, so this model has no burn control -- hotter gives more alpha power gives hotter. That is not a numerical divergence but a consequence of the closure, and it is precisely what “a constant chi is not a predictive closure” looks like. ★<strong>The step is bounded by the electron-ion exchange time</strong>: the exchange reaches the operator explicitly, and a step longer than that time does not blow up -- it <strong>decouples the heat pair silently</strong> (measured on this case: the adaptive controller grew dt to 0.13 s and reported T_e = 11.8 keV beside T_i = 6.3 keV, with half the alpha power). So this case uses a fixed dt of 20 ms, and the page carries a cap at the exchange time whose count is reported in the readings."
 },
 "fylite:config": {
  "geometry": "miller",
  "ch-heat": true, "ch-density": false, "ch-current": false,
  "dt": 0.02, "nsteps": 400, "dttarget": 0, "nlev": 31,
  "te0": 8.0, "ti0": 8.0, "peakt": 1.5, "peakn": 0.4,
  "edgete": 3.0, "edgeti": 3.0, "edgene": 3.0, "vloop": 0,
  "pe": 16.5, "pi": 16.5, "dep": 0, "depw": 0.35, "fuel": 0,
  "alpha": true, "brem": true, "ohmic": false, "bootstrap": false,
  "icd": 0, "zeff": 1.2, "species": "Be", "cimp": 1.65, "dtfrac": 0.375,
  "closure": "0", "chiratio": 1.0, "dchi": 0.3, "pinch": 0, "dpc": 0,
  "useref": false, "sawtooth": false, "sawmix": 1.20,
  "ip": 15000, "couple": 0, "relax": 0.5,
  "chi0": 0.6, "ne0": 10.0, "amin": 2.0, "rmaj": 3.1,
  "kappa": 1.70, "delta": 0.34, "q95": 3.0, "bunit": 5.3
 }
}
